 rtunity. LoG is distinct from LOD/AIS. Size M is an editorial estimate.\n
 Scope: Learning on graphs and geometry: graph neural networks\, equivaria
 nt models\, graph kernels\, geometric and graph generative models\, and s
 tatistical theory for structured data. Graph signal processing\, causal g
 raph models\, robustness\, and scalable graph-learning infrastructure are
  meaningful extensions. A graph or geometric contribution should remain c
 entral\, even in an application such as language or molecular modeling.\n
 Additional topics: Complex Systems & Network Science\, Probabilistic\, Ca
 usal & Uncertainty ML\, Signal Processing\, Robustness & Safety\, ML Syst
 ems & Infrastructure\nScope sources (2026): https://logconference.org/cfp
 /\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://logconference.org/
LOCATION:Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA
END:VEVENT
